Z||000000||Steven||03-05-2001||04:55 PM||||Well, today I was playing with the dyno program, and I was wondering if any one knew what I had to type in for the cam specs on a stock 2.8 liter? I think that the intake lift is .394, and the exhaust lift is .410, but what i don't know is when the intake and exhaust opens and closes. Any ideas? TIA.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Nashco||03-06-2001||07:59 PM||||Steven, do you have the cam files?  If you have the cam files you can just use the plugin for a cam that says it's basically stock.  If you have that you can try out a few different cams.  Here's the settings for the most basic "factory-style" cam I have listed:<P>Cam #:  Chevy 16-115-4 V6 <BR>Lifter Type:  Hydraulic<BR>Timing Spec @:  Seat-To-Seat<BR>Intake lift: 0.390<BR>Exhaust lift: 0.390 <BR>IVO:12.0    IVC:  48.0    EVO:  52.0   EVC:16.0 <BR>Engine:Chevy V6 (2.8-3.4L) 1979-94 <BR>Application:  Street <BR>Description:  Works well with stock computer & fuel injection. Very good for stock rebuild. <BR>File Creator:  Competition Cams <BR>Part Number:  16-115-4 Hyd V6<P>Hope this helps, good luck!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
